.TH ACER\-SENSE 1 "September 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acer\-sense \- control panel for Acer Predator and Nitro laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acer\-sense
.SH DESCRIPTION
A PredatorSense\-like interface built on the linuwu_sense driver and on
.BR power\-profiles\-daemon (8).
.PP
It opens with the laptop's dedicated key, which the package sets up during
installation, or from the applications menu.
.SH PAGES
.TP
.B Monitoring
CPU, GPU, system and NVMe temperatures, fan speed shown as turning blades,
battery state, power draw and CPU frequency.
.TP
.B Fans
The embedded controller's automatic mode, a manual percentage with the real
speed alongside, or an editable curve: drag the points to set the temperature
at which the fans start and how steeply they ramp up.
.TP
.B Keyboard
Backlight effect, brightness, speed, direction and colour, plus a fixed colour
per zone. The zones are picked on a drawing of the keyboard rather than from a
list, so it is clear which one is which.
.TP
.B Power
System power profile, panel refresh rate, and powering the NVIDIA GPU up or
down while the system is running.
.TP
.B Battery and system
80% charge limit, calibration, USB charging while the machine is off, LCD
override and boot animation.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The firmware exposes no fine\-grained frequency or voltage control: what Acer
calls overclocking is Turbo mode, which has two states and is triggered by the
physical button on the laptop.
.PP
The battery charge limit is fixed at 80% by the firmware and takes no other
value.
.PP
On the PH315\-53 the firmware answers only five of the eight backlight
effects. The three it ignores are shown greyed out rather than hidden, so it is
clear they exist but this machine will not play them.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Driver settings need membership of the
.B linuwu_sense
group, which the package grants to the installing user. Log out and back in for
it to take effect.
.PP
If the application reports a permission error while you are already in that
group, the sysfs attributes have lost their ownership, which happens whenever
the module is reloaded. A udev rule restores it; to fix it by hand without
logging out:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo systemd\-tmpfiles \-\-create /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/linuwu\-sense.conf
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acer\-powersave (1),
.BR blink (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Antonio Orizondo Leyva
